<title>UK: SKB Banka GDRs admitted to London Stock Exchange.</title>
<headline>SKB Banka GDRs admitted to London Stock Exchange.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Global depository receipts (GDRs) in SKB banka, Slovenia's second-largest bank, were admitted to the London Stock Exchange on Monday February 10, the Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>A total of 1,300,000 GDRs, representing 65,000 ordinary shares, were admitted. A total of $17.0 million was raised with the issue.</p>
<p>The Stock Exchange said SKB Bank was the first Slovenian company to gain a listing in London.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7945</p>
